From 107187a5f470484a85db21e42e8c0a7803af7354 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:02:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 174/174] nvhost-ctrl: a wait during the last one's signal
 waits it out; the null renderer locked

A syncpoint's host action signals its event and only then marks it
Signalled. The guest thread it woke could make its next fence wait on
the same event in between: libnx takes the lowest free slot each time.
That wait was refused as BadParameter, and libnx's nvFenceWait returns
the error without waiting. The program went on as if the GPU had got
there.

gputest closed its channel and freed its framebuffer while the GPU
still had two frames of clears for it: a SIGSEGV at exit, about 1 run
in 8 on one core with the GPU thread split, whose back end signals.
Traced: the wait for the last fence was never armed. The Signalling
state lasts moments, so EventWait and FreeEvent wait it out. 45 runs
on one core after the fix, none crashed.

The null renderer's software draws (queued draws, their textures'
cache) are now behind a recursive mutex. The emulated CPU's threads
reach them too: device memory unmapped or written (InvalidateRegion),
read (FlushRegion). The Vulkan rasterizer locks its caches for the same
reason. Callbacks (fences, syncpoints) run outside the lock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VdsH7Cki1YqWbFL1ncEV7C
